<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Media (region)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Media was an ancient region of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> mountains and the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecbatana">Ecbatana</a>, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamadan">Hamadan</a>. Home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a>, it was the core of the Median kingdom of the seventh and sixth centuries BCE and then a rich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapy</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> it was divided, the north becoming the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/media-atropatene">Media Atropatene</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/media-region.jpg" alt="Media (region)" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adrien-Hubert Brué · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brue,_Adrien_Hubert,_Asie-Mineure,_Armenie,_Syrie,_Mesopotamie,_Caucase._1839._(CG).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
